WEBVTT

00:01.750 --> 00:03.770
<i>We are on the 3rd day of the tournament.</i>

00:03.770 --> 00:09.670
<i>The first games have ended in every venue, and the 32 teams have started their second games.</i>

00:09.670 --> 00:10.320
Here!

00:10.320 --> 00:13.290
<i>Matsuoka MS is closing in on Hirado's side.</i>

00:13.290 --> 00:14.570
I won't let you, y'know!

00:14.570 --> 00:17.080
<i>Jito from Hirado goes to mark them.</i>

00:17.080 --> 00:20.330
<i>His fierce dash is just like a rushing truck!</i>

00:20.330 --> 00:21.870
To the left!

00:21.870 --> 00:24.920
I said I won't let you, y'know!

00:24.920 --> 00:26.390
<i>No, they can't pass through.</i>

00:26.390 --> 00:28.130
<i>Jito completely clears the ball.</i>

00:28.130 --> 00:30.880
<i>Hirado's defense is sure strong.</i>

00:30.880 --> 00:33.880
<i>Hirado has yet to concede a goal in this tournament.</i>

00:33.880 --> 00:35.730
<i>This is nothing.</i>

00:35.730 --> 00:40.140
<i>I won't show you our true power until we play against Nankatsu.</i>

00:40.770 --> 00:43.520
<i>At that time, the first match of the day was being held at Saitama World Stadium:</i>

00:43.520 --> 00:51.110
<i>The second match between Akita's Hanawa MS, and Yamanashi's Sakimoto MS.</i>

00:51.110 --> 00:53.360
All right! They got the ball to the twins!

00:53.360 --> 00:56.700
This time, make sure to show us your real football.

00:57.220 --> 00:57.820
Bro!

00:58.340 --> 00:59.080
All right!

00:59.080 --> 01:01.370
<i>The older brother Masao Tachibana who is being marked,</i>

01:01.370 --> 01:04.090
<i>crosses the ball to his younger brother, Kazuo.</i>

01:04.090 --> 01:05.160
Like I'd let it pass!

01:05.160 --> 01:06.960
<i>No, it's not for him!</i>

01:06.960 --> 01:09.530
<i>It was a pass for Ono, passing over Kazuo!</i>

01:09.530 --> 01:10.290
Go!

01:11.370 --> 01:12.840
<i>Goal!</i>

01:12.840 --> 01:14.420
<i>It's another goal for Hanawa!</i>

01:14.420 --> 01:19.140
<i>Even though Hanawa didn't show us Tachibana Twins' specialty, mid-air football,</i>

01:19.140 --> 01:21.140
<i>this goal has sealed their opponent's fate.</i>

01:21.140 --> 01:24.200
It looks like they are saving their mid-air football for later.

01:24.200 --> 01:27.400
Damn it! So they won't show us what they've got, huh?

01:28.650 --> 01:31.900
Look forward to our brand new move tomorrow.

01:33.070 --> 01:34.530
All right! We did it!

01:34.530 --> 01:36.610
<i>The final whistle blows!</i>

01:36.610 --> 01:38.100
<i>The score's 2-0.</i>

01:38.100 --> 01:40.620
<i>Hanawa advances to the third round!</i>

01:40.620 --> 01:46.000
<i>They will be playing against the winner of the next match, Nankatsu vs. Nishikigaoka.</i>

01:46.440 --> 01:48.540
All right, it's our turn next.

01:48.540 --> 01:50.000
Yes sir!

01:52.260 --> 01:54.970
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:52.260 --> 01:54.970
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:55.880 --> 01:58.550
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:55.880 --> 01:58.550
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:59.470 --> 02:02.180
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:59.470 --> 02:02.180
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:09.060 --> 02:11.900
<i>moeru you ni hitori demo</i>

02:09.060 --> 02:11.900
<i>I keep running, lying to myself</i>

02:11.900 --> 02:18.160
<i>ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete</i>

02:11.900 --> 02:18.160
<i>that I can live alone, though the loneliness makes me burn</i>

02:18.160 --> 02:24.040
<i>unubore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta na no ni</i>

02:18.160 --> 02:24.040
<i>You knew how fragile my self-conceit makes me</i>

02:24.040 --> 02:30.630
<i>kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni</i>

02:24.040 --> 02:30.630
<i>In this night that even shattered my heart</i>

02:30.630 --> 02:34.630
<i>kimi no koe sagasu</i>

02:30.630 --> 02:34.630
<i>I hate how weak I am</i>

02:34.630 --> 02:39.140
<i>kono yowasa ga nikui yo</i>

02:34.630 --> 02:39.140
<i>yearning for your voice</i>

02:39.140 --> 02:44.680
<i>ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya</i>

02:39.140 --> 02:44.680
<i>"I've got to get you back right now!"</i>

02:44.680 --> 02:46.270
<i>baka darou?</i>

02:44.680 --> 02:46.270
<i>I'm stupid, right?</i>

02:46.270 --> 02:47.480
<i>ai</i>

02:46.270 --> 02:47.480
<i>Love!</i>

02:47.480 --> 02:50.980
<i>kizudarake no ai wo shinjite</i>

02:47.480 --> 02:50.980
<i>Believing in my scarred love</i>

02:50.980 --> 03:00.870
<i>nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete</i>

02:50.980 --> 03:00.870
<i>I will turn these shedded tears into strength</i>

03:00.870 --> 03:01.700
<i>ai</i>

03:00.870 --> 03:01.700
<i>Love!</i>

03:01.700 --> 03:05.500
<i>kizudarake no ai da to shite mo</i>

03:01.700 --> 03:05.500
<i>Even though it is a scarred love</i>

03:05.500 --> 03:09.500
<i>bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru</i>

03:05.500 --> 03:09.500
<i>it lightens up our world</i>

03:09.500 --> 03:15.760
<i>kono ai mo ichido taritomo</i>

03:09.500 --> 03:15.760
<i>I will not let go of this love</i>

03:15.760 --> 03:18.550
<i>hanasanai</i>

03:15.760 --> 03:18.550
<i>for a single moment!</i>

03:20.380 --> 03:25.390
<b><b>EPISODE 37:
SKYLAB HURRICANE!</b></b>

03:20.970 --> 03:23.970
<i>Both teams' players take their positions on the field.</i>

03:23.970 --> 03:25.720
<i>Today's second game will be</i>

03:25.720 --> 03:30.980
<i>the second match for both Shizuoka's representative, Nankatsu, and Kanagawa's representative, Nishigaoka.</i>

03:30.980 --> 03:35.070
<i>As you already know, Nankatsu, along with their Captain Tsubasa,</i>

03:35.070 --> 03:40.030
<i>are the favorites for the champion's title, continuing the tradition from these past two years.</i>

03:40.030 --> 03:45.700
<i>Their opponents, Nishikigaoka, beat Kochi's representative Ozusan by a score of 3-1,</i>

03:45.700 --> 03:47.450
<i>and they are on a roll.</i>

03:47.450 --> 03:50.790
<i>Can Nishikigaoka be a giant killer and beat Nankatsu?</i>

03:50.790 --> 03:54.290
Let's watch and study carefully for tomorrow's game.

03:54.290 --> 03:55.810
Tsubasa!

03:55.810 --> 03:58.420
Keep scoring today, too!

04:03.530 --> 04:05.140
<i>Tsubasa...</i>

04:07.730 --> 04:09.600
We made it in time, y'know.

04:09.600 --> 04:11.850
<i>The game will start with Nankatsu's kick-off.</i>

04:11.850 --> 04:13.480
All right, let's do this!

04:15.560 --> 04:16.560
Here you go!

04:19.320 --> 04:22.330
Tsubasa, your leg is still hurt.

04:22.330 --> 04:24.950
You can rest today until the push comes to shove!

04:24.950 --> 04:26.320
You heard him!

04:26.320 --> 04:29.180
We'll be depending on you when things get serious.

04:29.790 --> 04:31.120
Let's go, guys!

04:31.120 --> 04:32.120
Yeah!

04:33.350 --> 04:38.360
<i>It looks like Nankatsu will be attacking with Izawa as the play-maker, and not Tsubasa.</i>

04:38.360 --> 04:41.380
What? Tsubasa won't do it?

04:41.380 --> 04:43.510
Damn it! They are underestimating us!

04:43.510 --> 04:47.600
<i>You</i> are underestimating us by thinking that Nankatsu is just about Tsubasa!

04:48.660 --> 04:52.870
<i>Izawa passes through a player, and sends a long pass to the front line after breaking through.</i>

04:52.870 --> 04:53.560
Take that!

04:53.560 --> 04:55.730
<i>Nagano sends it back to the other side.</i>

04:56.520 --> 04:58.540
<i>The ball is accurately sent to Taki.</i>

04:58.540 --> 05:00.850
<i>Will Taki dribble, as he loves to do?</i>

05:00.850 --> 05:02.280
It's on you, Izawa!

05:02.280 --> 05:04.530
<i>No, he sent it to the middle of the field again!</i>

05:04.530 --> 05:06.110
See this to its end,

05:06.110 --> 05:07.090
Kisugi!

05:07.090 --> 05:09.740
<i>Izawa skillfully sends the ball in front of the goal!</i>

05:09.740 --> 05:12.870
<i>Kisugi, who ran there in that time, connects!</i>

05:13.770 --> 05:15.110
<i>Goal!</i>

05:15.110 --> 05:17.080
<i>Nankatsu scores a brilliant first goal!</i>

05:17.080 --> 05:19.060
All right!

05:17.610 --> 05:21.710
<i>It's thanks to Taki, Izawa and Kisugi's superb combination play.</i>

05:23.590 --> 05:26.190
You did it! Ex-Shutetsu Trio!

05:26.190 --> 05:28.760
Going good, Taki! Izawa! Kisugi!

05:29.920 --> 05:30.810
Guys...

05:34.660 --> 05:35.520
<i>All right!</i>

05:35.520 --> 05:37.280
You think I'd let you?

05:37.280 --> 05:38.850
<i>Ishizaki clears the ball!</i>

05:39.540 --> 05:42.070
<i>Nankatsu's working hard on their defense too.</i>

05:42.070 --> 05:44.410
<i>Okay! It looks like everyone's in good shape today.</i>

05:44.410 --> 05:46.820
<i>They're at their best, except for Tsubasa.</i>

05:46.820 --> 05:48.320
Okay, go!

05:50.060 --> 05:50.910
Fall back!

05:50.910 --> 05:52.580
<i>Nankatsu once again moves to attack!</i>

05:52.970 --> 05:54.830
<i>Nishikigaoka is scrambling back!</i>

05:54.830 --> 05:55.960
All right!

05:58.550 --> 05:59.990
<i>It's in!</i>

05:59.990 --> 06:04.380
<i>A great long shot from Izawa, who used the gap in their opponent's defense.</i>

06:04.380 --> 06:05.460
I did it!

06:05.460 --> 06:08.560
Damn Nankatsu! They are playing without Tsubasa!

06:08.560 --> 06:10.110
Even then, they're still strong.

06:10.110 --> 06:14.600
Even if Tsubasa's not there, everyone has considerable offensive and defensive power.

06:14.600 --> 06:17.170
Nankatsu is as good a team as we expected.

06:17.170 --> 06:20.350
They don't seem to have any glaring weaknesses.

06:20.350 --> 06:22.970
Ever since we were called the favorites to win the championship,

06:22.970 --> 06:25.860
all eyes have been on us, especially Tsubasa.

06:25.860 --> 06:28.340
There's no point in hiding what we've got now.

06:28.340 --> 06:30.870
We'll let you see all of our skills.

06:34.960 --> 06:39.290
Even though we've kept our new special move a secret until now to put pressure on Nankatsu,

06:39.290 --> 06:45.420
they are just showing their full force plainly and putting pressure on us!

06:46.360 --> 06:47.420
Get this one, Taki!

06:47.420 --> 06:48.220
Sure thing!

06:48.220 --> 06:50.590
<i>Nankatsu doesn't hold back when they attack!</i>

06:50.590 --> 06:52.590
<i>Will it be the third goal right away?</i>

06:52.590 --> 06:54.430
What?

06:55.090 --> 06:56.310
Tsubasa...

06:57.180 --> 06:58.100
Take this!

06:58.770 --> 07:00.290
<i>Goal!</i>

07:00.290 --> 07:03.400
<i>The one who scored the third goal for Nankatsu is Tsubasa!</i>

07:03.400 --> 07:04.940
Tsubasa!

07:06.240 --> 07:09.470
Well, if I rest too much, I'll get rusty, you know.

07:09.470 --> 07:11.320
Let me do this much at least.

07:11.320 --> 07:12.930
Get a load of this guy!

07:12.930 --> 07:14.950
We told you it was ok for you to rest!

07:14.950 --> 07:17.240
Oh well, you're the lead player after all.

07:17.240 --> 07:19.250
That's our Tsubasa!

07:19.250 --> 07:20.560
He's so cool!

07:20.560 --> 07:23.330
Kumi, you really do only watch Tsubasa, don't you?

07:23.330 --> 07:25.330
<i>Tsubasa...</i>

07:27.250 --> 07:29.670
<i>The game ends with this whistle.</i>

07:29.670 --> 07:31.070
<i>6-0!</i>

07:31.070 --> 07:33.760
<i>Nankatsu shows their power as the reigning champions.</i>

07:33.760 --> 07:36.460
<i>They move on to the third match.</i>

07:36.460 --> 07:37.950
They sure are strong.

07:37.950 --> 07:40.020
We were no match for them.

07:40.020 --> 07:43.270
All right! Next in line is Hanawa!

07:43.270 --> 07:45.980
Just you wait, Tachibana Twins!

07:45.980 --> 07:47.810
You're strong, Nankatsu...

07:47.810 --> 07:49.740
That's how we like it!

07:51.510 --> 07:53.570
<i>It's the fourth day of the tournament.</i>

07:53.570 --> 07:59.020
<i>Aiming for their third championship, Nankatsu wakes up to the morning of their match against Hanawa,</i>

07:59.020 --> 08:02.040
<i>the second big obstacle in their path after Azumaichi.</i>

08:02.530 --> 08:04.750
It looks like it'll be a hot day.

08:09.940 --> 08:11.630
All right!

08:11.630 --> 08:19.060
Fight! Fight!

08:25.410 --> 08:29.320
<i>No matter what happens, I'll find a way to play in the finals.</i>

08:29.940 --> 08:34.070
<i>So guys, please keep winning until the final.</i>

08:34.490 --> 08:35.250
Captain...

08:35.250 --> 08:36.700
Hyuga...

08:36.700 --> 08:38.990
Hey, who said you could take a break?

08:38.990 --> 08:41.170
Keep running!

08:41.170 --> 08:42.600
Yes!

08:42.600 --> 08:51.300
Fight! Fight!

08:52.780 --> 08:57.680
<i>Saitama World Stadium is fired up even before the games start.</i>

08:57.680 --> 09:01.850
<i>The first game today is the third round match between Nankatsu MS and Hanawa MS.</i>

09:01.850 --> 09:04.620
Good luck, good luck, Hanawa!

09:02.540 --> 09:07.840
<i>Just for this match, Hanawa has brought more than double the number of their cheering squad from Akita.</i>

09:07.840 --> 09:12.370
<i>They are that serious about taking down the favorite of this tournament, Nankatsu.</i>

09:12.370 --> 09:14.610
Those cheers are something.

09:14.610 --> 09:16.610
HANAWA MIDDLE SCHOOL
AKITA PREFECTURE

09:15.750 --> 09:16.610
Listen, boys!

09:16.610 --> 09:20.370
Even if it's just to respond to their cheers, make sure you win!

09:20.370 --> 09:21.370
Yeah!

09:21.370 --> 09:23.120
NANKATSU MIDDLE SCHOOL
SHIZUOKA PREFECTURE

09:22.100 --> 09:25.210
Okay guys. Don't forget yesterday's rhythm.

09:25.210 --> 09:26.910
Today, give it all you've got!

09:26.910 --> 09:27.830
Yes sir!

09:32.070 --> 09:33.880
It's been a while, Tsubasa.

09:33.880 --> 09:34.730
Yeah.

09:34.730 --> 09:36.590
The elementary school tournament, wasn't it?

09:36.590 --> 09:39.930
It's been that long. We were looking forward to this since the drawings.

09:39.930 --> 09:44.650
Unlike yesterday, today we'll show you all of our strength.

09:44.650 --> 09:47.900
I'm sory, but your unbroken win-streak will end today.

09:47.900 --> 09:50.500
Hmph, as if we'd let you have your way.

09:50.500 --> 09:53.900
Your mid-air football has no effect on us.

09:55.060 --> 09:57.590
You are still in hight spirits as ever, I see.

09:57.590 --> 10:00.180
I expect another own-goal from you, Mr. Monkey!

10:00.180 --> 10:01.660
What did you say?

10:01.660 --> 10:04.870
I have changed, okay?

10:02.300 --> 10:04.870
Are they still going on about that?

10:04.870 --> 10:08.710
<i>Players of both teams have come out on the field.</i>

10:09.720 --> 10:12.250
<i>The spectators fire up!</i>

10:12.250 --> 10:13.590
Hanawa!

10:13.590 --> 10:15.760
Go for the win, Hanawa!

10:15.760 --> 10:18.260
We're counting on you today as well, Nankatsu!

10:23.350 --> 10:25.220
I trust you with the pictures.

10:25.220 --> 10:28.410
Can he really shoot a Drive Shot?

10:28.410 --> 10:31.530
Even though it's Tsubasa, he's still a middle schooler.

10:31.530 --> 10:35.050
Moreover, he didn't shoot one in the Nishikigaoka match.

10:35.050 --> 10:36.960
Today, he very likely will.

10:36.960 --> 10:37.570
Wha—

10:38.140 --> 10:39.820
Call it a journalist's intuition.

10:40.720 --> 10:45.900
<i>At the same time, at Bay Coast Stadium, Tokyo's Toho Academy and Gifu's Yoko MS</i>

10:45.900 --> 10:50.790
<i>were about to begin their third match.</i>

10:51.300 --> 10:53.960
Hyuga is not on the bench today either.

10:53.960 --> 10:57.140
So we won't get to see his fearsome kick.

10:57.140 --> 11:01.210
Maybe he really isn't feeling well; maybe he's injured.

11:01.210 --> 11:04.640
If they wanted to save him for the finals, they could keep him on the bench.

11:04.640 --> 11:06.060
If that's the case...

11:06.060 --> 11:08.310
Sorry for being abrupt,

11:08.310 --> 11:09.600
KOJIRO HYUGA ON THE BENCH!!
AN EXPLOSIVE POWER DWELLS IN HIS RIGHT LEG!!
ARE THEY SAVING HIM FOR THE FINALS!?
THE HOLE IN THE STADIUM'S WALL CREATED BY HYUGA'S SHOT

11:08.310 --> 11:11.600
but wasn't that article made-up?

11:10.400 --> 11:11.600
KOJIRO HYUGA ON THE BENCH!!
AN EXPLOSIVE POWER DWELLS IN HIS RIGHT LEG!!

11:11.600 --> 11:14.110
No, it was all true.

11:15.560 --> 11:17.690
<i>I saw it with my own eyes.</i>

11:17.690 --> 11:21.710
<i>That's right, it was a miraculous shot.</i>

11:21.710 --> 11:25.280
<i>It was more than two times faster than a normal player...</i>

11:25.280 --> 11:27.460
<i>A dream-like shot.</i>

11:32.910 --> 11:37.170
<i>It's the Tiger Shot of the Ferocious Tiger, Kojiro Hyuga!</i>

11:38.800 --> 11:42.020
Don't let your guard down just because you scored 8 goals yesterday.

11:42.020 --> 11:43.440
Stay focused.

11:43.440 --> 11:44.470
Yes, sir!

11:44.470 --> 11:48.140
<i>Even if Hyuga is not here, we'll make our way until the finals.</i>

11:48.140 --> 11:52.920
<i>And if our coach says that he won't let Hyuga play in the finals,</i>

11:52.920 --> 11:56.880
<i>we will boycott the match!</i>

12:05.640 --> 12:10.750
<i>The match everyone's been waiting for, Nankatsu versus Hanawa, is about to start.</i>

12:11.420 --> 12:14.850
<i>Let me introduce each team's starting members.</i>

12:14.850 --> 12:16.000
<i>First up is Hanawa.</i>

12:16.880 --> 12:19.020
<i>Yoshikura is at goalkeeping position.</i>

12:19.020 --> 12:23.720
<i>Koda, Takeda, Nakamura and Murasawa make up the defense.</i>

12:23.720 --> 12:27.720
<i>Shiota, Aimoto and Tamai at midfield.</i>

12:27.720 --> 12:32.370
<i>Ono and the Tachibana Twins with their acrobatic football,</i>

12:32.370 --> 12:34.900
<i>Masao and Kazuo Tachibana at forward.</i>

12:35.520 --> 12:38.650
<i>Let's continue with Nankatsu's starting members.</i>

12:39.480 --> 12:41.690
<i>Morisaki is the starting goalkeeper.</i>

12:41.690 --> 12:46.730
<i>Nakazato, Oda, Takasugi and Ishizaki make up the defense.</i>

12:46.730 --> 12:52.100
<i>Iwami, Izawa and their captain Tsubasa Ozora at midfield.</i>

12:52.100 --> 12:55.460
<i>Nagano, Kisugi and Taki at forward.</i>

13:01.970 --> 13:04.340
<i>The match starts with Nankatsu's kick-off!</i>

13:04.340 --> 13:05.950
Counting on you, Tsubasa!

13:05.950 --> 13:06.590
Sure!

13:06.590 --> 13:10.400
<i>Tsubasa didn't have any big moments in the second match,</i>

13:10.400 --> 13:13.770
<i>but he will be the playmaker for this important match.</i>

13:13.770 --> 13:16.080
It wouldn't be fun otherwise!

13:16.080 --> 13:17.400
Let's settle this Tsubasa!

13:18.330 --> 13:20.690
<i>So you're already coming, huh, Tachibana Twins?</i>

13:20.690 --> 13:29.700
Three years ago, you covered our attacks with Nankatsu's Golden Duo, Tsubasa and Misaki.

13:30.460 --> 13:33.700
But Nankatsu doesn't have Misaki anymore!

13:33.790 --> 13:38.160
In other words, right now, we are the strongest duo!

13:38.160 --> 13:39.450
Let's go Tsubasa!

13:39.450 --> 13:43.010
You won't be able to stop us all by yourself!

13:43.610 --> 13:46.130
<i>It's true: I don't have Misaki anymore.</i>

13:46.680 --> 13:49.970
<i>But even if I don't have Misaki, I still have...</i>

13:50.710 --> 13:54.480
<i>Tsubasa passes instead of trying to dribble past them!</i>

13:54.480 --> 13:55.180
What?!

13:56.140 --> 13:59.940
<i>...this many friends with me!</i>

14:00.450 --> 14:02.020
Let's go guys!

14:02.020 --> 14:03.240
Sure!

14:03.240 --> 14:06.410
<i>Nankatsu is advancing through Hanawa's side!</i>

14:06.410 --> 14:07.420
What?!

14:08.950 --> 14:09.700
Iwami!

14:09.700 --> 14:10.910
Izawa!

14:10.910 --> 14:15.700
<i>The ball is sent to Izawa who leads Nankatsu's midfield with Tsubasa.</i>

14:15.700 --> 14:16.210
Take it!

14:16.210 --> 14:18.330
<i>Izawa sends the ball to the wing quickly.</i>

14:18.330 --> 14:21.430
<i>Taki is waiting there, as per usual.</i>

14:21.430 --> 14:23.590
<i>Will he use his signature touchline dribble?</i>

14:23.590 --> 14:25.840
<i>No, he cuts towards the center!</i>

14:26.220 --> 14:27.300
Like I'd let you go!

14:28.760 --> 14:29.430
Wha–

14:29.430 --> 14:33.050
<i>Hanawa's defense is trying to stop him, but Taki switches to Kisugi!</i>

14:33.050 --> 14:34.520
Great, it was a success!

14:35.400 --> 14:38.520
<i>Kisugi dribbles along the side line without a pause.</i>

14:38.520 --> 14:39.270
Hey!

14:39.250 --> 14:41.690
<i>Hanawa's defenders are perplexed by this!</i>

14:39.270 --> 14:41.690
What are you doing?! Chase them!

14:42.420 --> 14:43.150
Here!

14:43.150 --> 14:45.030
<i>Kisugi sends it back to the middle.</i>

14:45.420 --> 14:47.740
<i>Tsubasa is making his way there.</i>

14:47.740 --> 14:50.870
Idiots! Don't leave Tsubasa unmarked!

14:50.870 --> 14:51.450
Taki!

14:51.450 --> 14:54.450
<i>Tsubasa made a great pass to the front of the goal!</i>

14:52.790 --> 14:54.450
Nice pass!

14:54.450 --> 14:56.950
<i>Taki is inside shooting range!</i>

14:56.950 --> 14:58.250
Eat this!

15:02.170 --> 15:04.060
<i>It's in!</i>

15:04.060 --> 15:05.270
I did it!

15:05.270 --> 15:07.550
<i>Nankatsu shows brilliant team play!</i>

15:07.550 --> 15:10.050
<i>Just one minute after the match's started.</i>

15:10.050 --> 15:14.010
<i>They score a precious opening goal, spoiling Hanawa's start!</i>

15:14.010 --> 15:15.600
We did it!

15:15.600 --> 15:18.180
<i>Good, you boys are doing well.</i>

15:18.180 --> 15:21.480
Doing awesome, Taki!

15:22.370 --> 15:24.100
Aw, man...

15:24.100 --> 15:25.650
Damn it!

15:25.650 --> 15:29.340
Okay then. It is time for our mid-air football!

15:29.340 --> 15:30.460
Let's go, Kazuo!

15:30.460 --> 15:31.410
Yeah!

15:34.330 --> 15:35.080
Masao!

15:35.480 --> 15:36.240
All right.

15:36.240 --> 15:37.740
Come with me, Masao!

15:37.740 --> 15:40.310
<i>Now it's Hanawa's turn to attack!</i>

15:40.310 --> 15:43.000
<i>The Tachibana Twins march forward with the ball.</i>

15:43.000 --> 15:45.790
Takasugi, Ishizaki! Mark those two!

15:45.790 --> 15:46.630
Sure!

15:46.630 --> 15:48.460
It won't go as you planned.

15:48.460 --> 15:49.460
Before you start...

15:49.460 --> 15:51.840
...our mid-air football has arrived!

15:51.840 --> 15:57.140
<i>Masao Tachibana sends the ball up high in the air to the front of the goal.</i>

15:57.140 --> 16:01.140
<i>Tachibana Twins' trademark, mid-air football is in motion!</i>

16:01.140 --> 16:03.650
It comes! The shot from that time...

16:06.480 --> 16:08.030
I'm going for it, Masao!

16:08.030 --> 16:11.030
Let's tie it first with our Triangle Shot!

16:11.030 --> 16:12.450
As if I'd let you!

16:12.450 --> 16:15.730
Didn't I say your mid-air football is not going to work?!

16:15.730 --> 16:16.570
What?!

16:16.570 --> 16:20.750
You can say that after you've seen what we're capable of!

16:20.750 --> 16:23.120
I said it's useless!

16:24.370 --> 16:27.000
<i>Kazuo Tachibana's lost his balance!</i>

16:27.000 --> 16:28.840
<i>He can't jump like that!</i>

16:30.380 --> 16:36.090
<i>Hanawa's mid-air football and the Tachibana Twins' Triangle Shot have been shot down!</i>

16:38.200 --> 16:40.640
Nice one! Well done Ishizaki!

16:40.640 --> 16:42.330
You are great, Ishizaki!

16:42.330 --> 16:46.360
Good job thinking that with your non-existent brain! That's a clever boy!

16:47.700 --> 16:51.900
You know, I still owed one for my own goal back then.

16:53.150 --> 16:55.300
Did you see that?

16:55.300 --> 17:01.290
I've always thought Ishizaki was undependable, but he does well at the right times.

17:01.290 --> 17:03.690
I'd never think they would be stopped in such a way.

17:03.690 --> 17:04.670
Yeah.

17:04.670 --> 17:06.870
Great, let's get on to this rhythm!

17:06.870 --> 17:08.170
Guys, let's get another goal!

17:08.660 --> 17:10.090
Let's put our backs into it!

17:10.090 --> 17:11.210
Here we go!

17:11.780 --> 17:14.640
<i>People expected this third match to be a derby match,</i>

17:14.640 --> 17:18.670
<i>but everything is moving along at Nankatsu's pace.</i>

17:18.670 --> 17:24.150
<i>Hanawa's defenders are perplexed by Nankatsu's non-stop attacks from the middle.</i>

17:24.150 --> 17:25.230
Damn!

17:26.590 --> 17:31.230
So even a surprise attack from Hanawa's Tachibana Twins won't be effective against Nankatsu

17:31.230 --> 17:36.740
They do some amusing stuff, but they had a weakness that was surprisingly easy to exploit, y'know.

17:36.740 --> 17:40.280
Our combination play does not have that weakness though.

17:41.930 --> 17:45.170
<i>Nankatsu's good form continues as they aim for another goal.</i>

17:45.170 --> 17:46.750
I'm leaving it to you all!

17:46.750 --> 17:50.880
<i>Tsubasa stands out among them, having completely discarded yesterday's self-effacing play.</i>

17:50.880 --> 17:54.880
<i>He is truly showing his true potential in every situation.</i>

17:54.880 --> 17:57.240
Tsubasa is moving quite well, today!

17:57.240 --> 18:01.590
Letting him rest during the second match seems to have worked out well for them.

18:01.590 --> 18:04.020
That's a different kind of teamwork I guess.

18:05.060 --> 18:05.770
There it goes!

18:05.770 --> 18:09.310
<i>The ball reaches Tsubasa, who is in top form today!</i>

18:11.190 --> 18:12.480
I'm going!

18:13.860 --> 18:15.440
<i>He is too swift!</i>

18:15.440 --> 18:18.160
<i>Tsubasa dashed through them in an instant!</i>

18:18.160 --> 18:19.450
You did it, Tsubasa!

18:19.450 --> 18:20.570
Damn it!

18:20.570 --> 18:24.540
<i>The third center-back Murazawa doesn't hesitate and dashes in!</i>

18:28.750 --> 18:34.190
<i>But now, Tsubasa's quickly turned himself
to the side and sends a pass!</i>

18:34.190 --> 18:35.210
What?!

18:35.210 --> 18:38.130
<i>The center forward Kisugi is running to get the ball!</i>

18:38.130 --> 18:43.390
<i>I'm Teppei Kisugi, the scorer! It would be shameful to not score this open chance!</i>

18:46.500 --> 18:47.910
<i>He scores!</i>

18:47.910 --> 18:50.440
<i>Nankatsu scores again early in the first half!</i>

18:52.190 --> 18:53.770
Nice shot, Kisugi!

18:53.770 --> 18:54.260
Right!

18:54.260 --> 18:55.050
We did it!

18:55.050 --> 18:56.690
Now, we are leading by two!

18:56.690 --> 18:57.890
Ugh...

18:57.890 --> 18:59.110
Second goal...

18:59.110 --> 19:01.580
<i>Hanawa has conceded two goals this early.</i>

19:01.580 --> 19:04.890
<i>I am sure they did not foresee this.</i>

19:04.890 --> 19:06.780
We have to do it, Kazuo.

19:06.780 --> 19:08.120
Yeah, big bro.

19:08.550 --> 19:10.850
We have no choice but to show that.

19:10.850 --> 19:13.570
Our new mid-air football that is.

19:15.520 --> 19:16.340
Guys!

19:16.340 --> 19:18.870
Sorry, Masao, Kazuo.

19:18.870 --> 19:20.470
Well, we can't change the past.

19:20.470 --> 19:22.970
What's important now is that we're counting on you, Ono.

19:23.550 --> 19:25.240
Send a cross up in front of the goal.

19:25.240 --> 19:27.240
So, you're going to do it?

19:27.240 --> 19:27.970
Yeah.

19:27.970 --> 19:29.730
Is it okay to do it?

19:29.730 --> 19:30.690
What about your legs?

19:31.810 --> 19:34.370
We've already come to terms with the strain it puts on our legs.

19:34.370 --> 19:37.940
We will score one back on them in this half, to start.

19:37.940 --> 19:41.520
<i>The match will resume with Hanawa's kick-off.</i>

19:41.520 --> 19:45.260
<i>Being behind by two goals against Nankatsu is proving to be harder than expected.</i>

19:45.260 --> 19:49.200
<i>We're hoping they will recover and attack like they've always done before.</i>

19:49.200 --> 19:52.570
Come at us from wherever you want!

19:52.570 --> 19:56.090
So long as I am here I won't let your mid-air football score.

19:56.090 --> 19:57.840
We are getting the third one!

20:01.000 --> 20:03.090
<i>What are they planning to do?</i>

20:04.020 --> 20:05.350
<i>The match resumes.</i>

20:05.860 --> 20:06.850
Let's go!

20:06.850 --> 20:07.850
Huh?

20:08.710 --> 20:13.270
<i>As soon as the whistle's blown, the Tachibana Twins move towards Nankatsu's goal without the ball!</i>

20:13.270 --> 20:17.190
<i>Ono takes the ball and is advancing up the wing.</i>

20:17.930 --> 20:18.860
Take it!

20:18.860 --> 20:21.610
<i>He quickly sends the ball up in front of the goal!</i>

20:24.610 --> 20:27.190
Hah, coming together won't change a thing.

20:27.190 --> 20:28.870
I will break your balance once again.

20:29.380 --> 20:31.040
Kazuo, now!

20:31.040 --> 20:31.660
Sure!

20:34.370 --> 20:35.450
What?!

20:35.450 --> 20:37.880
<i>What exactly is this?</i>

20:37.880 --> 20:41.630
<i>Masao Tachibana gets on his back and slides on the ground!</i>

20:41.630 --> 20:44.380
<i>What's this supposed to mean?</i>

20:44.380 --> 20:45.890
I am going for it, Masao!

20:46.800 --> 20:48.050
Sure!

20:48.810 --> 20:50.810
This is...!

20:51.850 --> 20:59.690
Go, our new mid-air football, Skylab Hurricane!

20:59.690 --> 21:11.180
<i>Oh my! The Tachibana Twins docked their feet together—
and one launches the other into the air!</i>

21:15.000 --> 21:18.210
Go!

21:18.210 --> 21:19.040
Morisaki!

21:19.040 --> 21:20.210
Yeah!

21:20.210 --> 21:22.660
<i>It's in!</i>

21:22.660 --> 21:26.940
<i>Here comes a mind-blowing new mid-air technique from Tachibana Twins!</i>

21:26.940 --> 21:28.720
This is...!

21:28.720 --> 21:32.140
<i>This is the very essence of the acrobatic football here!</i>

21:32.140 --> 21:38.230
<i>The debut of the new mid-air technique from Hanawa's Tachibana Twins, the Skylab Hurricane!</i>

21:39.730 --> 21:41.930
Finally, it's here!

21:41.930 --> 21:43.740
This match has just begun!

21:43.740 --> 21:47.160
You did it, Masao, Kazuo!

21:52.440 --> 21:54.240
What was that just now?

21:54.240 --> 21:55.830
Oh...

21:57.830 --> 22:00.180
Hah! Did you see that, Nankatsu?

22:00.180 --> 22:03.730
This is our new mid-air technique, Skylab Hurricane.

22:03.730 --> 22:04.840
We've paid one back!

22:04.840 --> 22:06.650
The match starts from this point on!

22:07.590 --> 22:10.110
<i>What an awesome technique...</i>

22:10.110 --> 22:12.970
<i>Skylab Hurricane...</i>

22:38.750 --> 22:44.800
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.750 --> 22:44.800
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.800 --> 22:50.800
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.800 --> 22:50.800
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.800 --> 22:56.850
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.800 --> 22:56.850
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:01.480
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:01.480
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:07.780
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:07.780
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.110 --> 23:15.200
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.110 --> 23:15.200
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.200 --> 23:21.250
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.250 --> 23:25.710
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.250 --> 23:25.710
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.010 --> 23:33.350
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.010 --> 23:33.350
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.350 --> 23:39.390
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.390 --> 23:45.690
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.390 --> 23:45.690
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.030 --> 24:00.570
COMING UP, EPISODE 38:
TAKE THEM DOWN! TACHIBANA TWINS
